# tests/mcp-resume, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it drives `caos mcp hook` the way Claude Code does, to pin what
# `/fork-caos-conversation <hash>` and `/resume-from-caos-conversation <hash>`
# do on a NEW session's first prompt: a fork is a new branch from the same
# commit, a resume appends to the SAME branch, and a head a session died on is
# used as it is (its open request closed on top of it) rather than refused.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/cli-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=.
